<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cacao">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cacao</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cacao is the tree native to tropical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesoamerica">Mesoamerica</a> whose beans are used to make chocolate. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> cacao beans were drunk by the elite as a frothy beverage and also served as a form of currency. They were among the tribute goods sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> from lowland provinces.</p></div>
